{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1296324-parlor-trick-examples","id":1296324,"title":"Parlor Trick Examples","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-03-12T20:30:16-07:00","id":1296324,"title":"Parlor Trick Examples","content":"The Parlor Trick Merit is a fun little effect. The merit gives a whole set of possibilities; however, I am wondering if anyone came up with any of their own they'd like to share!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1407-endlesskng","name":"EndlessKng","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-13T08:13:31-07:00","id":1296418,"title":"","content":"Unlocking doors and windows by giving them a firm kick or shove at an odd angle. Not sure what Spheres you'd need for it, but it's a very useful trick to be able to do with no roll or Paradox... naturally it's only going to work on ordinary household and office doors/windows, not the kind that have been built with serious security in mind. Although with a high enough Security skill perhaps you could justify it.<br /> <br /> EDIT: This would likely demand Forces 2 and Matter 1 or 2.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 03-21-2019, 07:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-13T13:42:29-07:00","id":1296497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1296324-parlor-trick-examples?p=1296418#post1296418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unlocking doors and windows by giving them a firm kick or shove at an odd angle. Not sure what Spheres you'd need for it, but it's a very useful trick to be able to do with no roll or Paradox... naturally it's only going to work on ordinary household and office doors/windows, not the kind that have been built with serious security in mind. Although with a high enough Security skill perhaps you could justify it.</div> </div> </div> </div>That actually could come in handy... at the clubhouse we use to larp, three windows are painted shut that should be able to open...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1407-endlesskng","name":"EndlessKng","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T03:09:26-07:00","id":1297191,"title":"","content":"Hair or a cape billowing in the wind is always a classic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-19T20:36:27-07:00","id":1298106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1296324-parlor-trick-examples?p=1297191#post1297191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hair or a cape billowing in the wind is always a classic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting... though if it's uncontrollable it's more of an Echo, I'd think. If you can make Fabio hair blowing at will, though, that would be fun. I can see an Ecstatic use that trick, actually...<br /> <br /> Mmm... now I kind of want to create a small list - one for each Tradition (including the Hollow Ones), Craft, and Convention. Feel free to add some in below. (Alternatively, if you have ideas that might fit another WoD Splat besides mage, include them as well... hell, even CoD ideas would be cooll!)<br /> <br /> Syndicate: I THINK I read an example where someone could twist their wrist and make a dime fall out. It's too small to mess up the entire economy, but could be useful if you want to make change more exact or are short a dime or two on the vending machine and the Iterators are behind on upgrading it to chip readers for a while.<br /> <br /> Will need to think about some others...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1407-endlesskng","name":"EndlessKng","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-20T04:54:17-07:00","id":1298122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EndlessKng</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1296324-parlor-trick-examples?p=1298106#post1298106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting... though if it's uncontrollable it's more of an Echo, I'd think. If you can make Fabio hair blowing at will, though, that would be fun. I can see an Ecstatic use that trick, actually...</div> </div> </div> </div>Well then obviously you don't make it uncontrollable. It's a parlor trick, because it billows on command.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Mmm... now I kind of want to create a small list - one for each Tradition (including the Hollow Ones), Craft, and Convention. Feel free to add some in below. (Alternatively, if you have ideas that might fit another WoD Splat besides mage, include them as well... hell, even CoD ideas would be cooll!) </div> </div> </div>Among Mages who smoke, having the puffs shaped in fantastical ways. I'm not even talking about smoke rings here. I'm talking truly astounding shapes. Hermetics that make the smoke look like dragons. Euthanatoi (and Hollow Ones) who blow smoke skulls. Cult of Ecstasy mages whose reefer smoke forms spiraling fractal patterns.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-20T07:22:03-07:00","id":1298137,"title":"","content":"Let's get cracking! A few conjuration and forces parlor Tricks:<br /> <br /> <br /> - <b>Apocalypse-Twinkie (Matter 2 + Prime 2)</b>: You can conjure a twinkie in your pocket. Really, if bad comes to worse, you won't need to go on a quest to find the last one. Bill Murray will thank you. Bonus: You'll always have food. Except it's only Twinkies. Or a breath mint? Really, the type of candy is yours to pick.<br /> <br /> - <b>The loaded hip-flask (Matter 2 + Prime 2)</b>: Notice how certain characters in movies always have that handy small hip-flask in their coat pocket to calm the nerves? Notice how it rarely ever gets shown as empty? Now you know why. Cheers.<br /> <br /> - <b>Think Fast! (Forces 2)</b>: On the more elegant side of forces tricks, this allows you to always catch whatever's (with non-hostile intent) tossed at you - in style and with a smug grin on your face.<br /> <br /> - <b>Spoopy Camera (Forces 3 + Prime 2)</b> : Ever notice how cameras creepily fail just at the important moment? Especially when you thought you *just* saw something move on it? That's your shtick. Timing your trick right, a camera you've spotted will lose its picture quality for just a moment. Classic VHS tape seeking problems, or sudden digital artifacts on modern cameras..they happen just at the wrong time, and for but a moment, but it's enough to get you by. The problem? You need to actually spot the camera first and time it right to paint the short error onto the image taken in as you slip by quickly...don't overuse this either.<br /> <br /> - <b>Goddamn Tinitus! (Forces 3 + Prime 2)</b>: Yeah, there's that person in the room, and you just don't want them to hear you as you mutter the Important Passphrase to your friend. You *know* that darn person is evesdropping. Except...there goes that goddamn tinitus. For just a moment, there is that familiar (short) high pitch that only they can hear. Annoying. And gone again very soon, but it might be the thing that just have stopped them from hearing properly what they shouldn't hear...<br /> <br /> <br /> These spoiler'd ones are denied after discussion, because being either actually potentially paradox-without-witnesses, or combat related (Parlor Trick pretty much says 'non-combat in general):<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">- <b>Who's there!? (Might actually be outside Parlor Trick range - see posts Below. TL;DR: Potentially paradox)</b>: The bad guys have you in their sights. Or you are trying to avoid those sights? Orrrrr... they already captured you. Things look grim! If only they weren't paying attention to you as you reach for your strikingly yellow utility-belt.... And suddenly, the nearby foliage rustles! The sounds of steps come down that other corridor! A sound of something in the next room falling on the floor! Whatever you have specialized for (and remember, you gotta pick one of them..), it is not real, but <i>they</i> don't know that - and it's just the distraction you needed.<br /> <br /> - <b>So clumsy, Jackie would be proud (Denied, Parlor Trick says non-combat):</b> Akin to the certain magick-enhanced martial arts moves explained in HdydT - except the only thing you can do is fall down. You have mastered the art of slipping and falling <i>just in time</i> to dodge the hurt, giving you just the extra speed you needed to get out of that dead aim. You can't pull this off often. You can't do it while lounging leaned against a bar or on a rough carpet. But during a sudden rush of panic-action, these subtle forces might be the only thing giving you that little extra edge to get out of harm's way. Bonus: You will, of course, land ruffled but unharmed. Don't stress your luck. (Hey, the Parlor Trick entry only said no damage-<i>producing</i>...)</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 03-21-2019, 09:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-20T09:12:36-07:00","id":1298158,"title":"","content":"P.s. before this thread, I really only ever glimpsed at Parlor Trick and couldn't figure out any really good uses.<br /> But now I more and more see: Parlor Trick is really awesome once the creative juices get flowing. Seriously. We need a 1001 Parlor Tricks thread if other people get into gear.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-20T16:28:21-07:00","id":1298217,"title":"","content":"I don't think I've read the merit, so some of these may be too much or too little, but... <br /> <br /> Theme music that you can turn on and off. <br /> <br /> Turning pages of a book or opening unlocked doors or packing your suitcase telekinetically. Edit: the intent was choosing one of the three. Sorry for the confusion.<br /> <br /> Turning hair green with a touch. <br /> <br /> Conjuring dog residue.<br /> <br /> Making the sound of an annoying dog barking.<br /> <br /> Regurgitating food into its pre-eaten form (I don't know why you'd ever want to do this, but oh well.)<br /> <br /> Burping much louder than is normally possible.<br /> <br /> Blowing bubbles in comically large sizes and unusual shapes.<br /> <br /> Changing the color of a flame.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":20546,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/20546-dragonchild","user":"Dragonchild","date":". 03-21-2019, 05:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/20546-dragonchild","name":"Dragonchild","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-20T18:53:41-07:00","id":1298247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dragonchild</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1296324-parlor-trick-examples?p=1298217#post1298217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think I've read the merit, so some of these may be too much or too little, but...<br /> <br /> Theme music that you can turn on and off.<br /> <br /> Turning pages of a book or opening unlocked doors or packing your suitcase telekinetically.<br /> <br /> Turning hair green with a touch.<br /> <br /> Conjuring dog residue.<br /> <br /> Making the sound of an annoying dog barking.<br /> <br /> Regurgitating food into its pre-eaten form (I don't know why you'd ever want to do this, but oh well.)<br /> <br /> Burping much louder than is normally possible.<br /> <br /> Blowing bubbles in comically large sizes and unusual shapes.<br /> <br /> Changing the color of a flame.</div> </div> </div> </div>There isn't really a &quot;too little&quot; with them. It's too much that you have to be careful of (after all, it IS a repeatable paradox-free effect). And I don't think any of those are too much . The only one would be the &quot;telekinesis&quot; one - and that's only because it's three things in one. Each parlor trick should be a single effect - it can be a bit flexible (like the blowing bubbles example), but it has to be a singular, definable effect (one sentence without semicolons or independent clauses, is a good rule). But any of those individually would be good ones.<br /> <br /> Though... be careful of the flame one around Infernal-wise vampires and werewolves... turning it green could end your life in a hurry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1407-endlesskng","name":"EndlessKng","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-20T20:13:48-07:00","id":1298261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1296324-parlor-trick-examples?p=1298137#post1298137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- <b>Apocalypse-Twinkie</b>: You can conjure a twinkie in your pocket. Really, if bad comes to worse, you won't need to go on a quest to find the last one. Bill Murray will thank you. Bonus: You'll always have food. Except it's only Twinkies. Or a breath mint? Really, the type of candy is yours to pick.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Would you like a <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=mfisgGuuUD8\" target=\"_blank\">Jelly Baby</a>?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-20T20:27:45-07:00","id":1298263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1296324-parlor-trick-examples?p=1298137#post1298137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's get cracking! A few conjuration and forces parlor Tricks:<br /> <br /> <br /> - <b>Apocalypse-Twinkie</b>: You can conjure a twinkie in your pocket. Really, if bad comes to worse, you won't need to go on a quest to find the last one. Bill Murray will thank you. Bonus: You'll always have food. Except it's only Twinkies. Or a breath mint? Really, the type of candy is yours to pick.<br /> <br /> - <b>The loaded hip-flask</b>: Notice how certain characters in movies always have that handy small hip-flask in their coat pocket to calm the nerves? Notice how it rarely ever gets shown as empty? Now you know why. Cheers.<br /> <br /> - <b>Who's there!?</b>: The bad guys have you in their sights. Or you are trying to avoid those sights? Orrrrr... they already captured you. Things look grim! If only they weren't paying attention to you as you reach for your strikingly yellow utility-belt.... And suddenly, the nearby foliage rustles! The sounds of steps come down that other corridor! A sound of something in the next room falling on the floor! Whatever you have specialized for (and remember, you gotta pick one of them..), it is not real, but <i>they</i> don't know that - and it's just the distraction you needed.<br /> <br /> - <b>So clumsy, Jackie would be proud:</b> Akin to the certain magick-enhanced martial arts moves explained in HdydT - except the only thing you can do is fall down. You have mastered the art of slipping and falling <i>just in time</i> to dodge the hurt, giving you just the extra speed you needed to get out of that dead aim. You can't pull this off often. You can't do it while lounging leaned against a bar or on a rough carpet. But during a sudden rush of panic-action, these subtle forces might be the only thing giving you that little extra edge to get out of harm's way. Bonus: You will, of course, land ruffled but unharmed. Don't stress your luck. (Hey, the Parlor Trick entry only said no damage-<i>producing</i>...)<br /> <br /> - <b>Think Fast!</b>: On the more elegant side of forces tricks, this allows you to always catch whatever's (with non-hostile intent) tossed at you - in style and with a smug grin on your face.<br /> <br /> - <b>Spoopy Camera</b>: Ever notice how cameras creepily fail just at the important moment? Especially when you thought you *just* saw something move on it? That's your shtick. Timing your trick right, a camera you've spotted will lose its picture quality for just a moment. Classic VHS tape seeking problems, or sudden digital artifacts on modern cameras..they happen just at the wrong time, and for but a moment, but it's enough to get you by. The problem? You need to actually spot the camera first and time it right to paint the short error onto the image taken in as you slip by quickly...don't overuse this either.<br /> <br /> - <b>Goddamn Tinitus!</b>: Yeah, there's that person in the room, and you just don't want them to hear you as you mutter the Important Passphrase to your friend. You *know* that darn person is evesdropping. Except...there goes that goddamn tinitus. For just a moment, there is that familiar (short) high pitch that only they can hear. Annoying. And gone again very soon, but it might be the thing that just have stopped them from hearing properly what they shouldn't hear...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There's a couple of these on the edge of the power (Who's There is the one closest to being too much, if not over the line, but YMMV), but I definitely like the range and creativity. But I think Hip Flask and Think Fast are my two favorites from this list. I can see Hip Flash being useful for an Orphan on the streets or just a grizzled old mage of any order. And Think Fast feels like a Virtual Adept trick - it's them using what they THINK Kung Fu/Video Game Master reflexes SHOULD look like on an effortless level (an Akashic would likely come up with something slightly different... or just be able to do it naturally, honestly).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1407-endlesskng","name":"EndlessKng","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-20T22:20:23-07:00","id":1298271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EndlessKng</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1296324-parlor-trick-examples?p=1298247#post1298247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There isn't really a &quot;too little&quot; with them. It's too much that you have to be careful of (after all, it IS a repeatable paradox-free effect)</div> </div> </div> </div>I think even some of the official examples would turn paradox if being overused - pulling 30 roses out of a small pocket would start being awfully 'wtf'. Hence my 'Don't overuse this' comments with some of the examples - I think it goes for most Parlor Tricks in general.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EndlessKng</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1296324-parlor-trick-examples?p=1298263#post1298263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a couple of these on the edge of the power (Who's There is the one closest to being too much, if not over the line, but YMMV)</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Who's there?!&quot; might be indeed skirting the line - I've tried to make sure it only applies to a very specific sound (Corridor-steps won't help you if there is no corridor nearby, etc.), but yeah - while it technically fulfills all the requirements aside of not being very &quot;Sleight of hand&quot;, I think the only line it might *actually* cross is that a theoretical observer in the next room would notice that there was a sound without anything being there - that might be what pushes it over the line into a no-no paradoxial effect in a single use.<br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> I've actually Spoilertag-removed both, <b>'Who's there!?'</b> and <b>'So Clumsy'</b>, as the latter is combat related and Parlor Trick says 'non-combat' in general at the start, and the first definitely could be Vulgar Without Witnesses on even single-use.<br /> <br /> P.s. I still don't understand how changing hair color can be a parlor trick. Do you people know how much effort it is to get a new hair color right? D:","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 03-21-2019, 03:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-21T00:36:34-07:00","id":1298282,"title":"","content":"- <b>Windbreaker (Forces 2): </b>For those who think the ol' <i>&quot;lighting the cig without a match&quot;</i> is skirting it, here is a convenient alternative. Everybody hates it when you try to light something and there is just that darn gust of wind that keeps on putting out the lighter or match. Well, no more - just when you need it, the flame stays safe in just the right moment.<br /> <br /> - <b>Don't spit *and* don't swallow (correspondence 2 + Life 2 and/or Matter 2)</b> : Perhaps you are forced to take a drug to stay 'undercover'. Perhaps you are forced to take one, period. Or maybe you are just a specific kind of Cult Of Ecstacy member that doesn't want to ruin an expectation. Ahem. Either way, instead of ingesting whatever enters your oral cavities, it ends up in your pocket or nearby bag instead. It might be worth the later inconvenience.<br /> <br /> - <b>The lucky screen protector (Forces 2):</b> Okay. You *are* actually clumsy, but after paying way too much in hardware repairs over time, you've practiced this simple effect. Again and again.. now, if your favorite phone drops towards the ground from a normal height and you notice in time, it's safe. Lucky you! What brand *is* that?<br /> <br /> - <b>*Bang Bang* &quot;Yay!&quot; (Forces 2)</b>: There it goes again, that darn vending machine keeping something stuck. And banging on its front or side (usually) does not help. Except in your case. Whatever gets stuck, it always drops - and because you are extra lucky, you sometimes get a bonus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 03-21-2019, 09:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-21T01:00:46-07:00","id":1298283,"title":"","content":"- <b>*Click* (Forces 2 or Matter 2)</b>: Just what kind of Mage *are* you? Well, apparently the one who likes to play Russian Roulette. Literally. We're not even going to ask what crowd you are hanging with, but at some point you should feel bad about that thing never firing when it's your turn. Ever.<br /> <br /> - <b>God Of Gamblers (Correspondence 2 + Matter 2 | Forces 2 (depends on the game)</b>: A subtle turn of the dice. Always that luck with cards. That bumping the roulette ball does at just the last moment. There is that *one* game you specialize in where your odds are just better than everyone else's. WARNING: Repeated use can be hazardous to your health and/or result in bans from casino chains. Do not specialize in bowling unless you want to make The Dude sadface. NOTE: Forget about modern slot machines. Those are pimped with electronics and computers controlling everything.<br /> <br /> - <b>360 NoScope</b> / <b>&quot;AAA - 99999pts&quot; (Forces 2 + Time 1 (Highscore) or 2 (Competitive))</b>: The Virtual Adept variant of the above, and more aimed at competitive or HiScore videogames. Actually a subtle application of Forces (keyboard/Mouse/controller/arcade controls momvement - you have to pick one) and Time instead of anything electronics related. You darn cheater. Get ready for the 'LAME' brand.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 03-21-2019, 09:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-21T04:12:57-07:00","id":1298297,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6606_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6606\" data-vbnamecard=\"6606\">Ambrosia</a> these are beautiful, but it's worth remembering that you need to *possess* the necessary spheres. Therefore arguably the most important thing to do with these entries is say exactly what Spheres you need to get the trick. Would you mind editing your entries to add them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-21T04:19:41-07:00","id":1298298,"title":"","content":"- A neat trick where you can escape handcuffs, ties, plastic binds... easier to justify if you also exhibit hyperflexibility or have the Escapology ability. Might fail if someone goes to extreme lengths to ensure the trap/bind is ABSOLUTELY inescapable.<br /> <br /> Can be justified with Life 2 (very minor transformation of body to wiggle out), Correspondence 3 (if you can teleport, you can put a single part of your body into a position you'd struggle to reach otherwise), and others.<br /> <br /> - &quot;Of course I can show you my ID officer-&quot; This trick lets you pull an ID or business card from your pocket matching your current disguise, appearance or persona. This ID is functional for an average security guard, cop or traffic warden, it's one of those decent fakes that only looks bad on close inspection. To an onlooker it just looks like a neat trick dependent on preparation; obviously a person who pretends to be other people will carry fake identification!<br /> <br /> Can be justified with Matter 2 and Prime 2 for the conjuring of a small, simple object.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-21T05:53:41-07:00","id":1298305,"title":"","content":"&quot;hidden pocket&quot; or &quot;nothing under my sleeve&quot; (Mind 3 / Matter 2).<br /> <br /> Whenever you put clothes with pockets you can choose one. This pocket (and only this pocket) has a locked Mind 3 obfuscating effect that hiddes the pocket itself (and any small trinket you hide there up to the size of a cigarette box, more or less), giving onlookers the impresion that there's nothing to be seen there.<br /> <br /> This Trick doesn't fool electronic devices and doesn't work if someone sees you introducing something on the pocket (or if the character it's too careless). Also, it wouldn't protect against being systematically searched for hidden pockets - in those cases the onlooker will find the pocket, almost not believing that she could have missed it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-21T06:36:37-07:00","id":1298310,"title":"","content":"I have to say... those are awesome. But... I do have a quibble.<br /> There is no way that the Screen Protector one would ever not be vulgar!<br /> <br /> J/k... that one actually is a really good idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1407-endlesskng","name":"EndlessKng","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-21T09:39:40-07:00","id":1298349,"title":"","content":"Don't need no stinkin' badges- as long as you're in a position of some kind of authority over a sleeper you're talking to, you can pass off nearly anything as a symbol of said authority. <br /> <br /> Don't need no stinkin' matches- you can ignite any small piece of wood by striking it on something like a match. <br /> <br /> Don't need no stinkin' mattress- you can sleep anywhere, in any position and wake up feeling rested. This does not protect you from environmental damage, sleeping on a rock would not cause you to wake up feeling like crap, but sleeping in a fire will still burn you up without some sort of protection from fire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":20546,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/20546-dragonchild","user":"Dragonchild","date":". 03-21-2019, 12:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/20546-dragonchild","name":"Dragonchild","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}